 {
  "pdf_index": 69,
  "blocks": [
   {
    "bbox": [
     9.495986938476562,
     -3.6251630783081055,
     223.57000732421875,
     15.166749954223633
    ],
    "font": "MyriadPro-Semibold",
    "size": 9.166999816894531,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "Chapter 3  I  recursion\n44",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     9.5,
     35.11800765991211,
     317.38543701171875,
     75.9610366821289
    ],
    "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
    "size": 11.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "Which approach seems easier to you? The first approach uses a while \nloop. While the pile isn’t empty, grab a box and look through it. Here’s \nsome pseudocode:",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     18.5,
     83.30200958251953,
     271.166748046875,
     172.6206512451172
    ],
    "font": "Courier-Bold",
    "size": 9.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "def look_for_key(main_box):\n  pile = main_box.make_a_pile_to_look_through()\n  while pile is not empty:\n    box = pile.grab_a_box()\n    for item in box:\n      if item.is_a_box():\n        pile.append(item)\n      elif item.is_a_key():\n        print(\"found the key!\")",
    "is_code": true
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     9.5,
     181.97500610351562,
     327.8664245605469,
     209.9590301513672
    ],
    "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
    "size": 11.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "The second way uses recursion. Recursion is where a function calls itself. \nHere’s the second way in pseudocode:",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     18.5,
     217.302001953125,
     242.7959747314453,
     276.6276550292969
    ],
    "font": "Courier-Bold",
    "size": 9.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "def look_for_key(box):\n  for item in box:\n    if item.is_a_box():\n      look_for_key(item)    \nRecursion!\n    elif item.is_a_key():\n      print(\"found the key!\")",
    "is_code": true
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     9.5,
     286.1180114746094,
     317.33062744140625,
     391.9710998535156
    ],
    "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
    "size": 11.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "Both approaches accomplish the same thing, but the second approach \nis clearer to me. Recursion is used when it makes the solution clearer. \nThere’s no performance benefit to using recursion; in fact, loops are \nsometimes better for performance. I like this quote by Leigh Caldwell \non Stack Overflow:  “Loops may achieve a performance gain for \nyour program. Recursion may achieve a performance gain for your \nprogrammer. Choose which is more important in your situation!” \n(http://stackoverflow.com/a/72694/139117).",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     9.5,
     394.6330871582031,
     282.5364990234375,
     422.4740905761719
    ],
    "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
    "size": 11.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "Many important algorithms use recursion, so it’s important to \nunderstand the concept.",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     9.5,
     452.19500732421875,
     235.75640869140625,
     474.49700927734375
    ],
    "font": "MyriadPro-Bold",
    "size": 18.0,
    "color": 10690613,
    "text": "Base case and recursive case",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     9.5,
     485.6180114746094,
     256.136474609375,
     539.4630126953125
    ],
    "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
    "size": 11.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "Because a recursive function calls itself, it’s easy to write \na function incorrectly that ends up in an infinite loop. \nFor example, suppose you want to write a function that \nprints a countdown like this:",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     18.5,
     547.128662109375,
     68.65702819824219,
     556.128662109375
    ],
    "font": "Courier",
    "size": 9.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "> 3...2...1",
    "is_code": true
   }
  ],
  "images": [
   [
    268.2820129394531,
    422.48101806640625,
    341.7220153808594,
    513.6810302734375
   ]
  ]
 },
 {
  "pdf_index": 70,
  "blocks": [
   {
    "bbox": [
     135.01400756835938,
     0.14801597595214844,
     432.5003356933594,
     11.166749954223633
    ],
    "font": "MyriadPro-It",
    "size": 9.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "Base case and recursive case\n45",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     27.5,
     35.11800765991211,
     179.15365600585938,
     49.957008361816406
    ],
    "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
    "size": 11.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "You can write it recursively like so:",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     36.5,
     57.6286506652832,
     135.41986083984375,
     86.62669372558594
    ],
    "font": "Courier",
    "size": 9.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "def countdown(i):\n    print(i)\n    countdown(i-1)",
    "is_code": true
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     36.5,
     97.62467956542969,
     109.9435806274414,
     106.62467956542969
    ],
    "font": "Courier",
    "size": 9.0,
    "color": 2301728,
