     107.96402740478516
    ],
    "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
    "size": 11.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "This section covers the call stack. The call stack is an important \nconcept in general programming, and it’s also important to \nunderstand when using recursion.",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     9.5,
     110.62603759765625,
     296.50762939453125,
     138.46705627441406
    ],
    "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
    "size": 11.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "Suppose you’re throwing a barbecue. You keep a to-do list for the \nbarbecue, in the form of a stack of sticky notes.",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     70.49500274658203,
     141.12905883789062,
     313.0406494140625,
     155.9680633544922
    ],
    "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
    "size": 11.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "Remember back when we talked about arrays and lists,",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     88.49099731445312,
     154.13107299804688,
     317.5087890625,
     168.97007751464844
    ],
    "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
    "size": 11.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "and you had a to-do list? You could add to-do items",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     9.499992370605469,
     167.13308715820312,
     315.14154052734375,
     246.98216247558594
    ],
    "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
    "size": 11.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "anywhere to the list or delete random items. The \nstack of sticky notes is much simpler. When you \ninsert an item, it gets added to the top of the list. When \nyou read an item, you only read the topmost item, and it’s taken off \nthe list. So your to-do list has only two actions: push (insert) and pop \n(remove and read).",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     9.5,
     377.34100341796875,
     147.28268432617188,
     392.17999267578125
    ],
    "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
    "size": 11.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "Let’s see the to-do list in action.",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     9.5,
     526.9500122070312,
     323.5907287597656,
     554.9340209960938
    ],
    "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
    "size": 11.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "This data structure is called a stack. The stack is a simple data structure. \nYou’ve been using a stack this whole time without realizing it!",
    "is_code": false
   }
