 {
  "pdf_index": 72,
  "blocks": [
   {
    "bbox": [
     168.74000549316406,
     0.14801597595214844,
     432.5003356933594,
     11.166749954223633
    ],
    "font": "MyriadPro-It",
    "size": 9.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "The stack\n47",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     27.5,
     34.65399932861328,
     110.22599792480469,
     52.0
    ],
    "font": "MyriadPro-Bold",
    "size": 14.0,
    "color": 6513766,
    "text": "The call stack",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     27.499969482421875,
     54.97800064086914,
     340.28387451171875,
     82.9620132446289
    ],
    "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
    "size": 11.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "Your computer uses a stack internally called the call stack. Let’s see it in \naction. Here’s a simple function:",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     36.5,
     90.30500030517578,
     242.57199096679688,
     139.62767028808594
    ],
    "font": "Courier-Bold",
    "size": 9.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "def greet(name):\n    print(\"hello, \" + name + \"!\")\n    greet2(name)\n    print(\"getting ready to say bye...\")\n    bye()",
    "is_code": true
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     27.5,
     149.12100219726562,
     330.6873474121094,
     176.96202087402344
    ],
    "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
    "size": 11.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "This function greets you and then calls two other functions. Here are \nthose two functions:",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     36.5,
     184.30499267578125,
     241.27774047851562,
     203.63063049316406
    ],
    "font": "Courier-Bold",
    "size": 9.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "def greet2(name):\n    print(\"how are you, \" + name + \"?\")",
    "is_code": true
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     36.5,
     214.30197143554688,
     144.64755249023438,
     233.6276092529297
    ],
    "font": "Courier-Bold",
    "size": 9.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "def bye():\n    print(\"ok bye! \")",
    "is_code": true
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     27.5,
     243.12100219726562,
     284.24664306640625,
     257.9599914550781
    ],
    "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
    "size": 11.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "Let’s walk through what happens when you call a function.",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     174.74099731445312,
     280.80999755859375,
     196.281005859375,
     293.20001220703125
    ],
    "font": "MyriadPro-Bold",
    "size": 10.0,
    "color": 10690613,
    "text": "Note",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     38.09600067138672,
     298.156005859375,
     334.9530029296875,
     321.574462890625
    ],
    "font": "MyriadPro-Regular",
    "size": 9.5,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "To keep things simple, I’m only showing the calls to greet, greet2, and \nbye. I’m not showing the calls to the print function.",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     27.499977111816406,
     346.8210144042969,
     329.3197326660156,
     374.6620178222656
    ],
    "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
    "size": 11.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "Suppose you call greet(\"maggie\"). First, your computer allocates a \nbox of memory for that function call.",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     27.499977111816406,
     449.84100341796875,
     330.6650085449219,
     477.6819763183594
    ],
    "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
    "size": 11.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "Now let’s use the memory. The variable name is set to \"maggie\". That \nneeds to be saved in memory.",
    "is_code": false
   }
  ],
