 },
 {
  "pdf_index": 74,
  "blocks": [
   {
    "bbox": [
     168.74000549316406,
     0.14801597595214844,
     432.5003356933594,
     11.166749954223633
    ],
    "font": "MyriadPro-It",
    "size": 9.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "The stack\n49",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     27.5,
     35.11800765991211,
     338.3874816894531,
     62.957008361816406
    ],
    "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
    "size": 11.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "A box for that function is added to the top of the stack. Then you print \nok bye! and return from the function call.",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     27.5,
     158.77801513671875,
     343.6946105957031,
     199.61903381347656
    ],
    "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
    "size": 11.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "And you’re back to the greet function. There’s nothing else to be done, \nso you return from the greet function, too. This stack, used to save the \nvariables for multiple functions, is called the call stack.",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     27.639999389648438,
     213.38790893554688,
     88.73599243164062,
     228.13201904296875
    ],
    "font": "MyriadPro-Bold",
    "size": 12.90736198425293,
    "color": 10690613,
    "text": "EXERCISE",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     27.5,
     231.77801513671875,
     225.0506134033203,
     246.6170196533203
    ],
    "font": "MyriadPro-Bold",
    "size": 10.0,
    "color": 10690613,
    "text": "3.1  \u0007Suppose I show you a call stack like this.",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     27.5,
     328.6210021972656,
     310.9105529785156,
     343.4599914550781
    ],
    "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
    "size": 11.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "What information can you give me, just based on this call stack?",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     27.5,
     346.12200927734375,
     297.66424560546875,
     360.96099853515625
    ],
    "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
    "size": 11.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "Now let’s see the call stack in action with a recursive function.",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     27.5,
     372.65399169921875,
     202.27601623535156,
     390.0
    ],
    "font": "MyriadPro-Bold",
    "size": 14.0,
    "color": 6513766,
    "text": "The call stack with recursion",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     27.496994018554688,
     393.1210021972656,
     343.0590515136719,
     446.9620056152344
    ],
    "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
    "size": 11.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "Recursive functions use the call stack, too! Let’s look at this in action \nwith the factorial function. factorial(5) is written as 5!, and it’s \ndefined like this: 5! = 5 * 4 * 3 * 2 * 1. Similarly, factorial(3) is 3 * 2 * 1. \nHere’s a recursive function to calculate the factorial of a number:",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     36.49998474121094,
     454.30499267578125,
     163.5681915283203,
     505.1639709472656
    ],
    "font": "Courier-Bold",
    "size": 9.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "def fact(x):\n  if x == 1:\n    return 1\n  else:\n    return x * fact(x-1)",
    "is_code": true
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     27.5,
     513.1209716796875,
     345.4625244140625,
     553.9640502929688
    ],
    "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
    "size": 11.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "Now you can call fact(3). Let’s step through this call line by line and \nsee how the stack changes. Remember, the topmost box in the stack tells \nyou what call to fact you’re currently on.",
    "is_code": false
   }
  ],
